IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ma-s01-rescission`

-- Tests for ma-s01-rescission.l4.  Every expected value is written from the text of s 1 before the run:
-- "Where a person has entered into a contract after a misrepresentation has been made to him, and (a) the
-- misrepresentation has become a term of the contract; or (b) the contract has been performed, or both, then,
-- if otherwise he would be entitled to rescind the contract without alleging fraud, he shall be so entitled,
-- subject to the provisions of this Act, notwithstanding the matters mentioned in paragraphs (a) and (b)."

§ `Tests -- s 1(a) and (b)`

-- Either limb, or both, is enough.
#ASSERT `s 1(a) or (b) one or both of the matters mentioned in paragraphs (a) and (b) holds` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1(a) or (b) one or both of the matters mentioned in paragraphs (a) and (b) holds` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1(a) or (b) one or both of the matters mentioned in paragraphs (a) and (b) holds` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Neither limb holds: the "where" condition fails.
#ASSERT `s 1(a) or (b) one or both of the matters mentioned in paragraphs (a) and (b) holds` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A limb not given: one limb true settles it; otherwise the text decides nothing.
#ASSERT `s 1(a) or (b) one or both of the matters mentioned in paragraphs (a) and (b) holds` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1(a) or (b) one or both of the matters mentioned in paragraphs (a) and (b) holds` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1(a) or (b) one or both of the matters mentioned in paragraphs (a) and (b) holds` NOTHING (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1(a) or (b) one or both of the matters mentioned in paragraphs (a) and (b) holds` (JUST FALSE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1(a) or (b) one or both of the matters mentioned in paragraphs (a) and (b) holds` NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- s 1`

-- The misrepresentation has become a term of the contract (a), the contract not performed: entitled.
#ASSERT `s 1 the person is entitled to rescind notwithstanding the matters mentioned in paragraphs (a) and (b)` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The contract has been performed (b), not a term: entitled.
#ASSERT `s 1 the person is entitled to rescind notwithstanding the matters mentioned in paragraphs (a) and (b)` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "or both": entitled.
#ASSERT `s 1 the person is entitled to rescind notwithstanding the matters mentioned in paragraphs (a) and (b)` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Neither (a) nor (b): the "where" condition fails, s 1 gives no entitlement.
#ASSERT `s 1 the person is entitled to rescind notwithstanding the matters mentioned in paragraphs (a) and (b)` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- No contract entered into after a misrepresentation: the "where" condition fails.
#ASSERT `s 1 the person is entitled to rescind notwithstanding the matters mentioned in paragraphs (a) and (b)` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not otherwise entitled to rescind without alleging fraud: the "if" condition fails.
#ASSERT `s 1 the person is entitled to rescind notwithstanding the matters mentioned in paragraphs (a) and (b)` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A no stands whatever else was not given.
#ASSERT `s 1 the person is entitled to rescind notwithstanding the matters mentioned in paragraphs (a) and (b)` (JUST FALSE) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1 the person is entitled to rescind notwithstanding the matters mentioned in paragraphs (a) and (b)` NOTHING (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1 the person is entitled to rescind notwithstanding the matters mentioned in paragraphs (a) and (b)` NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not covered (a fact not given): NOTHING, never FALSE.
#ASSERT `s 1 the person is entitled to rescind notwithstanding the matters mentioned in paragraphs (a) and (b)` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1 the person is entitled to rescind notwithstanding the matters mentioned in paragraphs (a) and (b)` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1 the person is entitled to rescind notwithstanding the matters mentioned in paragraphs (a) and (b)` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- One limb given as true settles (a)/(b) even when the other is not given.
#ASSERT `s 1 the person is entitled to rescind notwithstanding the matters mentioned in paragraphs (a) and (b)` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
